<title>UK: BA Dec cargo load factor dips 0.3 pct.</title>
<headline>BA Dec cargo load factor dips 0.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways' said on Monday its overall cargo load factor dipped 0.3 percentage points in December to 67.9 percent compared with December 1995.</p>
<p>But BA's cargo tonne kilometres (CTKs) in December were 2.0 percent above the previous year lifting total mainline scheduled revenue tonne kilometres (RTKs) for the month by 7.2 percent on a total capacity growth (in available tonne kilometres, ATKs) of 7.6 percent.</p>
<p>Details of BA cargo statistics for December and the first nine months of the 1996/97 financial year with percentage changes from year ago figures include.</p>
<p>		    December		    Financial year</p>
<p>						    (Apr-Dec) to date</p>
<p>		   1996   1995   Pct	  1996    1995   Pct</p>
<p>				    Change			  Change</p>
<p>Revenue tonne km</p>
<p>(RTK) million</p>
<p>Cargo tonne     306    300   +2.0	 2842     2617  +8.6</p>
<p>km (CTK)</p>
<p>Total RTK	1095   1021   +7.2	10671    10010  +6.6</p>
<p>Available	1612   1498   +7.6	15070    14030  +7.4</p>
<p>tonne km million</p>
<p>Overall pct    67.9   68.2   -0.3 pts   70.8     71.3  -0.5 pts</p>
<p>load factor</p>
<p>TOTAL GROUP SCHEDULED SERVICES</p>
<p>(including Deutsche BA, TAT)</p>
<p>Total RTK (m)  1110   1034   +7.3	10821    10135  +6.8</p>
<p>RTK million</p>
<p>Available     1646   1529   +7.7	 15396    14307  +7.6</p>
<p>tonne million *   ATK figures for mainline scheduled services for</p>
<p>the previous year have been restated to reflect improved calculation methodology.</p>
